{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"neutral-skyblue-hog","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\n`fixture_selection.select_from_corpus` eagerly compiles full ticket state for EVERY\nreview-bearing ticket before selection, via `reader(ticket_id, tracker)` (default\n`labels._read_ticket_state_via_env_override`, which calls `show_ticket(ticket_id,\ninclude_inbound=True)`). At full corpus scale this is ~6s/ticket x ~1957 unique tickets\n≈ **~3 hours of pure CPU** before a single candidate is emitted — and the live admission\nrunner (`fixture_admission`) pays this same cost upfront on every run.\n\nMeasured this session (impl-693 worktree, full committed corpus): a single\n`_read_ticket_state_via_env_override` call is ~5–7s; the selection loop compiled state for\n1957 unique tickets; a stubbed reader completes the identical candidate selection in ~57s.\n\n## Why it's expensive and why it's avoidable\n\n`ticket_state` is consumed in selection ONLY by `_escaped(review)` →\n`labels.escaped_defect(state)`, which needs just two things: `close_class == \"plan_defect\"`\nand any inbound `caused_by` link. The full `show_ticket(include_inbound=True)` reducer is far\nmore than that. The candidate SET and tier split are provably independent of ticket_state\n(tier derives from fire/no_fire signals: reproduction/author_response/margin); `escaped_defect`\nonly affects the rank tiebreak (2nd sort key in `_candidate_sort_key`).\n\nThe corpus event loader (`corpus._load_ticket_events`) does NOT carry STATUS/LINK events, so a\ncheap batched `escaped_defect` index cannot be built from it directly — the fix needs either a\nbatched store read of close_class + caused_by edges, or lazy per-ticket compilation restricted\nto only the tickets actually referenced by emitted candidates.\n\n## Approach\n\nCompile `escaped_defect` (or the minimal ticket_state it needs) lazily/batched instead of\neagerly for all review-bearing tickets:\n- Option A (lazy): defer state compilation until a review is about to become an emitted\n  candidate, so only the small candidate-referenced ticket set pays the cost.\n- Option B (batched): one store-wide pass building `{ticket: close_class}` and a reverse\n  `caused_by` index, then an O(1) `escaped_defect` lookup per ticket.\n\nPreserve behaviour: candidate set, tiers, ranks (incl. escaped-defect promotion) must be\nbyte-identical to the current eager path over the same committed history.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `select_from_corpus` over the full committed corpus completes in minutes, not hours,\n      with NO per-review-bearing-ticket `show_ticket(include_inbound=True)` fan-out — verified\n      by a test asserting the reader/compile is invoked only for candidate-referenced tickets\n      (or replaced by a batched index), not for all review-bearing tickets.\n- [ ] Emitted manifest rows (candidate set, tier, direction, rank, escaped_defect) are\n      byte-identical to the current implementation over a fixed fixture corpus — verified by a\n      regression test comparing old vs new output.\n- [ ] `escaped_defect` fidelity is preserved: a ticket closed `plan_defect`, and a ticket named\n      by an inbound `caused_by`, both still rank-promote — verified by a held-out test.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n      pass.\n\n## Provenance\n\nDiscovered during REB-693 (epic 65dd / spin-cub-usher) ticket 67aa AC10: the live admission\nrun's selection step took >54 min CPU and was on track for ~3h before the norm-less findings\neven reached the solver. The AC10 live run was completed with a stubbed `read_ticket_state`\n(escaped_defect=False) as a documented fidelity compromise (candidate set + tiers identical;\nrank tiebreak only); this ticket is the real-fidelity + performance fix.","id":"f0d1-b0cf-0690-4b3f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"select_from_corpus eagerly compiles ticket state for all review-bearing tickets (~3h at full scale)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788450474474272001,"uuid":"ca24a1e4-af82-4d2f-b065-5d1e04daf937"}